  triage:title "D4a table-driven permutation test covers only 8 of about 19 section-A matrix rows; the remaining rows are discrete tests rather than the single table the deliverable specified" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1310-r7 (PR #1310, AY.15 herdr-name-uniqueness, FINAL head 10bc123f8; report: PR #1310 issuecomment 5575994618). req-qa. Sprint doc D4a (docs/plans/phase-ay/sprint-AY.15-herdr-name-uniqueness.md:127) specifies one table-driven permutation test named unique_name_permutations covering the herdr-naming-test-matrix.md section-A rows. At 10bc123f8 that table covers 8 rows; the other section-A rows are covered by separate discrete tests. Matrix-row coverage is real (AC1 satisfied) but the specified test architecture was not followed as written. Correction: either fold the remaining section-A rows into the unique_name_permutations table or amend D4a to record the discrete-test split explicitly." ;
